.TH NETSHIELD 1 "2026" "netshield-dns" "NetShield DNS Resolver"
.SH NAME
netshield \- control the NetShield DNS resolver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netshield
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netshield
talks to the running \fBnetshield-dns\fR service over its control socket
(\fI/run/netshield/control.sock\fR). The socket is accessible to root and to
members of the \fBnetshield\fR group.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show state, upstream, rule counts and query statistics.
.TP
\fBpause\fR [\fITIME\fR]
Stop blocking for \fITIME\fR (seconds, or with an m/h/d suffix; default 5m).
.TP
.B resume
Resume blocking immediately.
.TP
.B sync
Download the blocklists listed in \fIsources.list\fR now.
.TP
.B reload
Re-read \fInetshield.conf\fR, \fIrules.conf\fR, \fItrusted.list\fR and the cached blocklists.
Changes to \fBlisten_address\fR or \fBport\fR require a service restart.
.TP
.B flush
Clear the response cache.
.TP
\fBcheck\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR
Explain how the resolver would treat a domain.
.TP
\fBlogs\fR [\fIN\fR]
Show the last \fIN\fR queries (default 20).
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/netshield/netshield.conf
Main configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/netshield/rules.conf
Custom block / allow / map rules.
.TP
.I /etc/netshield/sources.list
Blocklist download URLs.
.TP
.I /etc/netshield/trusted.list
Domains exempt from blocking and limits.
.TP
.I /var/log/netshield/queries.log
Query log (if enabled).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
